{{also|люди}}
==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sh|sla-pro|*ljudъ||people, men}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sh}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁lewdʰ-}}.

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m|head=љу̑ди|c|ljȗdi}} (singular: {{l|sh|sc=Cyrl|чо̏вјек}} / {{l|sh|sc=Cyrl|чо̏век}})

# [[people]], [[men]]
#: Два '''човјека''' су ишла цестом — ''Two '''men''' walked down the street.''
#: Пет '''људи''' је ишло цестом. — ''Five '''people''' walked down the street.''

====Declension====
{{sh-decl-noun|sc=Cyrl
|чо̏вјек|љу̑ди
|човјека|љу́дӣ
|човјеку|људима
|човјека|људе
|човјече|људи
|човјеку|људима
|човјеком|људима}}

====Usage notes====
This plural form takes suppletive stem in the singular, as can be seen in the declension table. Old dual forms have been preserved in the counting for 2, 3, 4 (also in 11, 12, 13, 14 etc.) which bind plural form of {{m|sh|sc=Cyrl|чо̏вјек}} / {{m|sh|sc=Cyrl|чо̏век}}.

